Patch 7910 (experimental, rollback netcode): cellGcm_io_mapping(i, &ea, &size), a read-only accessor for the GCM IO mappings.

The rollback snapshot (installer/port/jsp/jsp_snapshot.cpp, used only with JSP_ROLLBACK=1) leaves RSX-visible main memory out of its save
and restore, because the RSX thread reads those pages while the game runs. Returns -1 past the table, 0 for an unused slot, 1 with (ea, size).
No behaviour change: nothing calls it unless the port does. Applies after 2001 (its context lines are 2001's accessors).

diff --git a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
index 16c43af..3ecab89 100644
--- a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
+++ b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
@@ -4649,6 +4649,17 @@ void cellGcmInitDefaultFifoMode(s32 mode)
 u32 cellGcm_default_context_ea(void)  { return s_gcm_context_ea; }
 u32 cellGcm_context_slot_ea(void)     { return s_gcm_ctx_out_ea; }
 
+/* Patch 7910: IO mapping slot i as (EA, size), for the port's snapshot diagnostic
+ * (jsp_snapshot.cpp), which must leave RSX-visible main memory alone. -1 past the table, 0 for an
+ * unused slot, 1 when filled. Read-only. */
+int cellGcm_io_mapping(u32 i, u32* ea, u32* size)
+{
+    if (i >= CELL_GCM_MAX_IO_MAPPINGS) return -1;
+    if (!s_io_mappings[i].active || !s_io_mappings[i].size) return 0;
+    *ea = s_io_mappings[i].ea; *size = s_io_mappings[i].size;
+    return 1;
+}
+
